WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.001 --> 00:00:07.963
- A thousand days ago,

00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:08.796
- Yes.

00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:10.698
- A few moons.

00:00:10.698 --> 00:00:12.658
I was, you know, I was like, debt,

00:00:12.658 --> 00:00:14.274
I was living off credit cards.

00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:17.243
This is better than any
50,000 person festival--

00:00:17.243 --> 00:00:18.348
(crowd cheering)

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:20.144
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael,

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:21.455
my one word is believe,

00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:23.863
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:23.863 --> 00:00:26.121
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:26.121 --> 00:00:27.341
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:28.174
today we're going to learn

00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:31.207
from Grammy Award-winning
music producer, Skrillex

00:00:31.207 --> 00:00:34.093
and my take on his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:34.093 --> 00:00:36.112
Rule number five is my personal favorite

00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:38.539
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:40.078
And as always, as you're listening

00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:41.825
if something really resonates with you,

00:00:41.825 --> 00:00:44.141
if there's a message that
really holds true to you,

00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:45.759
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:48.615
and put it in quotes so that
other people can be inspired

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.258
and when you write it down,
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:53.027
with yourself as well.

00:00:53.027 --> 00:00:53.860
Enjoy.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.435
- [Man] Give us a bit of insight into,

00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:17.251
were you sort of playing
smaller club shows?

00:01:17.251 --> 00:01:19.860
I know you released stuff
through a thing called Myspace

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.180
back in the day

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.263
and how that evolved, tell
us about that journey.

00:01:58.378 --> 00:01:59.974
- You look back and be
like, "I set those days,

00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:02.174
"I met some people, it was fun."

00:02:02.174 --> 00:02:03.174
That's cool.

00:02:13.363 --> 00:02:16.280
(electronic music)

00:02:21.754 --> 00:02:24.441
(screaming)

00:02:24.441 --> 00:02:27.108
(crowd roaring)

00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:35.933
Anything you're trying to start up,

00:02:35.933 --> 00:02:37.617
businesses or whatever, like,

00:02:37.617 --> 00:02:39.490
if you have a friend,
start it with a friend.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.098
The first guy that should hear your stuff,

00:02:41.098 --> 00:02:43.223
who should be excited about your stuff,

00:02:43.223 --> 00:02:45.081
is the guy that supports
you the most anyway.

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:46.607
And, like, maybe you can do it together

00:02:46.607 --> 00:02:48.239
and then that friend has another friend

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:49.375
and you bring them over and you say,

00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:50.723
"Hey, check this out, do you like this?"

00:02:50.723 --> 00:02:51.855
Maybe they don't like it

00:02:51.855 --> 00:02:53.248
and you find the next person

00:02:53.248 --> 00:02:54.357
and it literally, like,

00:02:54.357 --> 00:02:57.190
it's like you take one brick
and just stack the next

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.123
and the most you can do yourself,

00:02:59.123 --> 00:03:00.210
then you can create something.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.061
And sooner or later
people are going to notice

00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:03.061
what you're doing

00:03:03.061 --> 00:03:04.530
because they can feel that energy,

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.595
they can feel that, like,

00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:08.309
I mean, I think a lot of people,

00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:09.450
like A &amp; R in the industry,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.794
like part of what we look for in artists

00:03:10.794 --> 00:03:12.552
is not only someone that makes great music

00:03:12.552 --> 00:03:13.841
but is someone that has that energy,

00:03:13.841 --> 00:03:15.612
that devotion to what they're doing.

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.347
And that's a big thing,

00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:19.586
I mean, that's what I look
for in artists that I sign

00:03:19.586 --> 00:03:20.935
are people that are really talented

00:03:20.935 --> 00:03:22.264
and people that have that energy,

00:03:22.264 --> 00:03:24.933
like I'm just going to do a "What's up?"

00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:29.605
- A lot of your hardcore
fans were not really excited

00:03:29.605 --> 00:03:31.680
about this collaboration
with Justin Bieber.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.282
- I wouldn't even say a
lot of my hardcore fans,

00:03:33.282 --> 00:03:35.906
I think my hardcore fans get what I do

00:03:35.906 --> 00:03:38.083
and like the fact that I don't care

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.532
and I'm not, you know,

00:03:40.532 --> 00:03:43.910
I'm not afraid to fail or I'm
not afraid to do something

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.222
that everyone doesn't like.

00:03:45.222 --> 00:03:47.876
A lot of times, you know,
people do music for a long time

00:03:47.876 --> 00:03:48.862
then they get to a certain age,

00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:50.918
and you know, they have
families, they have kids,

00:03:50.918 --> 00:03:52.549
and all this stuff, but, like,

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:56.366
you know, we're just so
inspired and hungry to,

00:03:56.366 --> 00:03:59.820
like he said, make great
songs and make great tracks

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.702
that sound like nothing else

00:04:00.702 --> 00:04:02.877
and push the boundaries of what...

00:04:02.877 --> 00:04:04.177
I mean, even the Justin Bieber single,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.240
that's a top ten record,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.241
you know, isn't a pop format,

00:04:08.241 --> 00:04:09.543
the way it's written, you know?

00:04:09.543 --> 00:04:10.727
It's not a traditional pop song

00:04:10.727 --> 00:04:13.229
and it's trying to, sort of changing,

00:04:13.229 --> 00:04:15.975
not necessarily the
verse-chorus-verse-chorus-bridge-outro,

00:04:15.975 --> 00:04:17.902
it's like we're changing this sort of,

00:04:17.902 --> 00:04:19.243
the pop format.

00:04:19.243 --> 00:04:20.773
It was only a couple years ago,

00:04:20.773 --> 00:04:23.789
before, I'd say skip
back to three years ago,

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:25.261
like, I'm in debt.

00:04:25.261 --> 00:04:26.594
I'm probably in,

00:04:28.004 --> 00:04:29.024
like, $50 grand.

00:04:29.024 --> 00:04:29.857
- Three years ago?

00:04:29.857 --> 00:04:30.690
- Yeah, three years ago.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.891
- Like, 1,000 days.

00:04:31.891 --> 00:04:33.705
- Yeah, exactly, 1,000 days ago.

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:34.889
Yes.

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:36.488
(laughing)

00:04:36.488 --> 00:04:38.140
I was, like, you know, debt,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.365
I was living off credit card,

00:04:39.365 --> 00:04:41.806
like, I had spent some,

00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:43.335
I got this lease on this building

00:04:43.335 --> 00:04:44.485
that I was actually essentially trying

00:04:44.485 --> 00:04:45.883
to do the same thing I'm doing now,

00:04:45.883 --> 00:04:46.778
but this was three years ago,

00:04:46.778 --> 00:04:50.212
and it was so whack, and, like, not legit.

00:04:50.212 --> 00:04:53.045
But I built out 10,000 square feet

00:04:54.431 --> 00:04:56.811
of studio space as well,

00:04:56.811 --> 00:04:58.539
and this is me and my friends
living in this warehouse

00:04:58.539 --> 00:05:00.213
that wasn't zoned for living,

00:05:00.213 --> 00:05:01.715
so a year later we got kicked out.

00:05:01.715 --> 00:05:02.842
I was in so much debt.

00:05:02.842 --> 00:05:05.896
Skrillex started to go and I
was just paying off my debts

00:05:05.896 --> 00:05:10.063
and trying to, like,
re-stabilize myself, I guess.

00:05:11.817 --> 00:05:13.899
And I remember and one point
I had a million dollars

00:05:13.899 --> 00:05:16.784
in my account, and that was it,

00:05:16.784 --> 00:05:17.965
and we were doing this tour

00:05:17.965 --> 00:05:21.068
and all the shows were selling out.

00:05:21.068 --> 00:05:22.235
It was my first nation-wide tour

00:05:22.235 --> 00:05:24.123
and I spent all that money on production.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.523
Like, I was like, okay, cool,

00:05:25.523 --> 00:05:27.978
I just want to make all these
shows really really special

00:05:27.978 --> 00:05:31.177
and I want to make a show
that everyone remembers

00:05:31.177 --> 00:05:33.086
and I want to show that,

00:05:33.086 --> 00:05:35.409
show people that may not
necessarily know where we come from

00:05:35.409 --> 00:05:37.811
that it's more than just meets the eye,

00:05:37.811 --> 00:05:39.059
it's more than just pressing a button.

00:05:39.059 --> 00:05:42.021
There's so much that goes
into creating a great show.

00:05:42.021 --> 00:05:43.460
So, I spent all my money on that.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.771
Didn't have anything past that point,

00:05:45.771 --> 00:05:47.163
didn't really know what
I was going to be doing

00:05:47.163 --> 00:05:48.406
or what the thing was,

00:05:48.406 --> 00:05:51.923
but, like, it's times like that where you,

00:05:51.923 --> 00:05:53.242
where you really truly
believe in something

00:05:53.242 --> 00:05:55.146
and you make that giant leap.

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:57.780
And those are always really surreal

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:58.913
and important times in your life.

00:05:58.913 --> 00:06:00.423
Kind of like opening a new chapter.

00:06:00.423 --> 00:06:02.460
Like you're moving to a different city,

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.077
or you're going 100% on a new idea.

00:06:06.077 --> 00:06:07.609
Those are always important, I think,

00:06:07.609 --> 00:06:08.683
as artists and creative people,

00:06:08.683 --> 00:06:09.516
to take those,

00:06:09.516 --> 00:06:11.787
especially when you have
the right people around you.

00:06:11.787 --> 00:06:13.861
The last thing I need to do

00:06:13.861 --> 00:06:15.444
is go forum-rolling

00:06:16.406 --> 00:06:20.573
and checking out what the
people are talking about me.

00:06:21.666 --> 00:06:24.550
I don't care and, you know,

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.784
a part of me wants to ask them,

00:06:27.784 --> 00:06:28.969
"What's wrong, man?

00:06:28.969 --> 00:06:30.052
"Why are you,

00:06:32.073 --> 00:06:34.104
"Should I not be allowed to do this?

00:06:34.104 --> 00:06:34.983
"This is what I love to do."

00:06:34.983 --> 00:06:36.088
I'm not doing anything wrong,

00:06:36.088 --> 00:06:38.683
I'm not, you know, killing babies

00:06:38.683 --> 00:06:40.569
or, you know, I'm not doing anything bad.

00:06:40.569 --> 00:06:41.896
Like, you don't have to like my music

00:06:41.896 --> 00:06:43.674
but do you have to,

00:06:43.674 --> 00:06:44.910
the thing that's hard on me is, you know,

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.020
it's a waste of time.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:46.937
But I mean,

00:06:47.963 --> 00:06:49.687
you get angry sometimes,

00:06:49.687 --> 00:06:52.069
but then that kind of washes away

00:06:52.069 --> 00:06:53.706
and then you just go, "Man, that sucks."

00:06:53.706 --> 00:06:55.970
I'm more interested when I
read things in message boards

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.025
and reviews, like, I want to hear good,

00:06:58.025 --> 00:06:59.825
I want to find out new cool things,

00:06:59.825 --> 00:07:01.443
I want to hear a new great song.

00:07:01.443 --> 00:07:02.957
I don't want to hear someone
trash-talking someone else.

00:07:02.957 --> 00:07:04.640
I'm not just, that's not discovering,

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.940
that's dictation, you know what I mean?

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.774
You're telling me to think a certain way,

00:07:09.774 --> 00:07:11.545
whereas, like, something more open-minded,

00:07:11.545 --> 00:07:13.873
like, it's going to make me want to grow.

00:07:13.873 --> 00:07:17.634
- [Katie] I read that your
parents were Scientologists,

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:18.730
your dad still is.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.096
But you are not.

00:07:20.096 --> 00:07:22.493
- No, um, I'm not a Scientologist

00:07:22.493 --> 00:07:25.059
but my dad does it for himself

00:07:25.059 --> 00:07:27.386
and it's something that's
helped him forever.

00:07:27.386 --> 00:07:29.680
- And why didn't you want to,

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.514
if both your mom and dad--

00:07:31.514 --> 00:07:34.386
- Well, I think the main part, it's like,

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.448
you dedicate so much of your time to it

00:07:36.448 --> 00:07:38.979
and my time was always spent doing music

00:07:38.979 --> 00:07:41.386
and I wouldn't have been
able to do what I'm doing now

00:07:41.386 --> 00:07:43.664
if I spent my time doing that.

00:07:43.664 --> 00:07:46.299
Everyone at some point
is just a guy or a person

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.474
but if you enable, if you give the gift,

00:07:48.474 --> 00:07:50.366
enable someone to help out

00:07:50.366 --> 00:07:52.197
and to be a part of something,

00:07:52.197 --> 00:07:53.614
I think that's amazing,

00:07:53.614 --> 00:07:55.538
like, enablers, that's a true leader.

00:07:55.538 --> 00:07:57.456
When you can enable
someone that's under you

00:07:57.456 --> 00:07:58.767
and give them a step.

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.133
Because you look around, man,

00:08:00.133 --> 00:08:01.901
there's a lot more geniuses than you,

00:08:01.901 --> 00:08:03.155
than meets the eye.

00:08:03.155 --> 00:08:04.322
And you're like, man, these kids,

00:08:04.322 --> 00:08:05.155
all these people around me,

00:08:05.155 --> 00:08:06.501
all my friends that have
been touring with me,

00:08:06.501 --> 00:08:08.443
just, like, before we were driving vans

00:08:08.443 --> 00:08:09.705
and trailers together, like,

00:08:09.705 --> 00:08:11.104
Getting $50 a show,

00:08:11.104 --> 00:08:14.086
making no money but
doing it all ourselves.

00:08:14.086 --> 00:08:15.301
And we were just kids doing that,

00:08:15.301 --> 00:08:17.221
and looking back at it now, like,

00:08:17.221 --> 00:08:19.086
had we had the internet

00:08:19.086 --> 00:08:21.104
and all these things we have now,

00:08:21.104 --> 00:08:22.888
back then it would have
been a different story

00:08:22.888 --> 00:08:24.235
but now that's true, you know.

00:08:24.235 --> 00:08:26.194
Now it's like, it's incredible.

00:08:26.194 --> 00:08:27.875
- Leaders don't have followers,

00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.274
leaders create other leaders.

00:08:29.274 --> 00:08:30.107
- Right.

00:08:30.107 --> 00:08:31.222
What sucks about the future

00:08:31.222 --> 00:08:32.714
is that anything could happen.

00:08:32.714 --> 00:08:33.976
The exciting thing about this ride

00:08:33.976 --> 00:08:36.774
is it's expect the unexpected,

00:08:36.774 --> 00:08:39.542
that's been this whole year for us.

00:08:39.542 --> 00:08:40.946
Anything really can happen

00:08:40.946 --> 00:08:42.926
as long as you work hard

00:08:42.926 --> 00:08:44.448
and we keep doing what we're doing.

00:08:44.448 --> 00:08:46.746
We're working hard but
we'd be working hard anyway

00:08:46.746 --> 00:08:49.496
because we love the music, right?

00:08:55.466 --> 00:09:00.133
This is better than any
50,000 person festival.

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.883
(crowd cheering)

00:09:13.798 --> 00:09:15.881
You know what that means.

00:09:18.813 --> 00:09:21.230
No, no, no, wait, wait, wait.

00:09:29.988 --> 00:09:32.278
Every time I trainwreck a
mix or do something wrong

00:09:32.278 --> 00:09:34.294
I'm playing Indiana Jones.

00:09:34.294 --> 00:09:37.961
(Indiana Jones theme music)

00:10:18.894 --> 00:10:20.262
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:20.262 --> 00:10:21.118
I made this video

00:10:21.118 --> 00:10:23.596
because The Electric
Warehouse asked me to.

00:10:23.596 --> 00:10:24.937
If there's someone
you'd like me to profile

00:10:24.937 --> 00:10:26.550
in the next top ten,

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:28.128
check out the link in the description

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.167
and go and cast your vote.

00:10:30.167 --> 00:10:32.182
I'd also love to know what
was your favorite message

00:10:32.182 --> 00:10:33.015
from this video?

00:10:33.015 --> 00:10:34.365
What did you learn from this video

00:10:34.365 --> 00:10:36.948
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:10:36.948 --> 00:10:38.597
in your life or in your business?

00:10:38.597 --> 00:10:39.918
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:10:39.918 --> 00:10:41.150
I'm really curious to find out.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.804
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Surge Wisdom.

00:10:43.804 --> 00:10:45.864
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:10:45.864 --> 00:10:48.915
Your One Word, and posting
eight different reviews,

00:10:48.915 --> 00:10:50.926
chapter-by-chapter, of the book,

00:10:50.926 --> 00:10:53.422
on your YouTube channel and
promoting it on Twitter as well.

00:10:53.422 --> 00:10:55.419
I really really appreciate the support

00:10:55.419 --> 00:10:57.350
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.768
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:58.768 --> 00:10:59.889
I believe in you.

00:10:59.889 --> 00:11:01.821
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:11:01.821 --> 00:11:05.549
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:11:05.549 --> 00:11:07.049
I'll see you soon.

00:11:13.158 --> 00:11:15.399
- If it's not fun, if
it's not a good time,

00:11:15.399 --> 00:11:16.884
if the party doesn't...

00:11:16.884 --> 00:11:18.266
Then I don't want, then don't do it,

00:11:18.266 --> 00:11:20.259
you know what I mean?

00:11:20.259 --> 00:11:23.125
It's not a job, it should
be something you enjoy.

00:11:23.125 --> 00:11:24.967
And to see it grow and have success,

00:11:24.967 --> 00:11:25.986
you just want to work harder

00:11:25.986 --> 00:11:28.403
and make it better, you know.

00:11:33.117 --> 00:11:34.754
When you're playing a show,

00:11:34.754 --> 00:11:38.156
the energy you get from the
stage is, like, indescribable

00:11:38.156 --> 00:11:40.953
and it's just this constant
feedback, you know?

00:11:40.953 --> 00:11:41.987
Like a cycle.

00:11:41.987 --> 00:11:43.188
And when you're in the studio with people,

00:11:43.188 --> 00:11:44.071
when you have good energy

00:11:44.071 --> 00:11:45.689
and people are having fun
and feeling the music,

00:11:45.689 --> 00:11:48.645
it inspires you to continue
to go down the right path.

00:11:48.645 --> 00:11:51.639
People stop moving then you're
not making the right sounds.

00:11:51.639 --> 00:11:54.473
- [Katie] Scientology gets
a terrible rep, you know?

00:11:54.473 --> 00:11:56.093
What do you make of that?

00:11:56.093 --> 00:11:57.887
- I think it's easy for
a religion like that

00:11:57.887 --> 00:11:58.981
to get a bad rep,

00:11:58.981 --> 00:12:00.491
because it's so sensationalized

00:12:00.491 --> 00:12:01.573
and people want to get clicks

00:12:01.573 --> 00:12:03.872
and people want to sell
magazines, at the end of the day.

00:12:03.872 --> 00:12:07.500
And like, you've got Tom
Cruise jumping on couches

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.868
and that's, like, you know, with Oprah,

00:12:09.868 --> 00:12:11.662
and that whole thing was, like, hilarious.

00:12:11.662 --> 00:12:13.512
Being an artist and knowing what it's like

00:12:13.512 --> 00:12:15.365
to be taken out of context

00:12:15.365 --> 00:12:18.460
or at least to be criticized
so much in the media,

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.132
it's like, what is their
intention at the end of the day?

00:12:20.132 --> 00:12:22.564
They're just trying to get a reaction

00:12:22.564 --> 00:12:26.796
and I think if you're doing
something that makes you happy

00:12:26.796 --> 00:12:29.129
and that's all that matters.

